# Tailscale Serve / Funnel → Docker

Jobby’s public MCP URL is **Tailscale HTTPS in front of Compose**. The app
still binds **container 3000**; the host publish is `.ports.yml` `compose-web`
(today **4700**). Funnel/Serve that still point at `127.0.0.1:3001` return **502**.

How: `.cursor/skills/tailscale-serve/SKILL.md`. Docker: `47-docker-first.mdc`.

## Mapping (mandatory)

```
Tailscale HTTPS
  :443 /mcp /api/mcp /sse /.well-known  → ChatGPT / Claude.ai (no port in the URL)
  :8443 / :8444                         → Cursor / QA (explicit port; ChatGPT rejects this)
        → http://127.0.0.1:<compose-web>     # from .ports.yml
                → container :3000
```

- Read `.ports.yml` **before** `tailscale serve` or `tailscale funnel`.
- Backend is always `http://127.0.0.1:<compose-web>`. Never `3001`, never
  container `3000`, never another project’s port.
- Compose must be up (`127.0.0.1:<compose-web>→3000`) **before** clients connect.

## Serve vs Funnel

| Mode | Who can reach it | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `tailscale serve` | Tailnet only | Cursor/Claude on another tailnet machine |
| `tailscale funnel` | Public internet | ChatGPT, Claude.ai, phones off-tailnet |

ChatGPT **requires Funnel** (public HTTPS). Serve is not enough.

## Do not steal OmniRoute

On this Mac, `:443` `/` is the OmniRoute gateway. ChatGPT and Claude.ai use
**this machine’s** `:443` **paths** (`/mcp`, `/api/mcp`, `/sse`, `/.well-known`)
— the connector URL is `https://<this-host>.<tailnet>.ts.net/mcp/<key>` with
**no port**. Do not retarget `:443` `/` to Jobby. `:8443` is MCP-only for
clients that accept a port (Cursor). `your-gateway:8443` is a different host.

## After Compose port moves

If `.ports.yml` `compose-web` changes, **reset Funnel/Serve the same day**.
Stale `:3001` mappings are a product outage, not a client bug.

## Secrets

Never paste a live `jb_…` key into chat, issues, or rules. Rotate any key that
was pasted. Verify with `/signin` (200) and `/api/mcp` Accept SSE — not with a
raw key in the URL.
